;; The Lonely Rover, easy (issue #60): the opening's crater and cargo, exactly (the rim comes down on the same crates), with the
;; doc's easy setting and a kinder set of numbers. Every one is a number fed into an unchanged formula, so the physics the player
;; learns is the same: a smaller (1 kWh) bank fills in a fifth of the time, the salvaged motor starts charging at 750 rpm, not 1,500,
;; the call may go out whenever the bank is full and warm (no waiting for the pre-dawn relay pass), bearings wear a quarter as fast
;; and a sleep runs ahead four times as fast. The Advanced constants (gravity, eta, the charging temperatures) stay the planet's.
(world lonely-rover-easy
  (scenario
    (title "The Lonely Rover, easy")
    (description "The same crater and cargo, kinder numbers: a 1 kWh bank, a motor that charges from 750 rpm, the call at any hour once the bank is full and warm, slower wear and faster sleep. The physics is the real physics.")
    (tuning (bank-capacity 0.2) (generator-cut-in 0.5) (call-any-time #t) (wear 0.25) (sleep-speed 4)))
  (map victoria)
  (rover (at 190.0 140.0) (heading 270))
  (place battery-bank cargo-crate (at 264.0 0 143.0))
  (place solar-panels cargo-crate (at 254.62 0 147.0))
  (place gas-cylinders cargo-crate (at 249.42 0 144.0))
  (place hand-tools cargo-crate (at 242.49 0 140.0))
  (place spares cargo-crate (at 233.83 0 135.0)))
